+
+We report Wilson 95% intervals and seed-paired comparisons against solo, using paired-bootstrap 95% confidence intervals (CIs; 2,000 resamples) and exact McNemar tests [wilson1927probable, mcnemar1947sampling, fagerland2013mcnemar, efron1979bootstrap]. **pp** means percentage points. These methods assume independent task units; shared vocabulary, prompts or hosted models may limit that assumption. At small samples, bootstrap intervals need not agree with exact tests. Each cell has 10–20 seeds and about seven uncorrected comparisons, so we emphasize effect sizes and intervals. Rows with failed calls are excluded; Study 1 has none.
 
